; Alpaca — AnimalDefinition data entry (gdd.md -> Data Schemas / Content Architecture).
; Roster row: roster.md -> Already-Defined Roster | Ruled: decisions.md -> D-43.
; Asset: Quaternius "Ultimate Animated Animal Pack", CC0 1.0 Universal — see
;   project/attribution/sources/quaternius_ultimate_animated_animals.tres.
; Source: source-content/assets/Ultimate Animated Animals - July 2021/glTF/Alpaca.gltf
;
; SPECIES: alpaca (Lama pacos).
;
; CAPACITY FIELDS (D-43, tiles_per_individual REVISED by D-45): capacity_radius = 0 ->
; SENTINEL `CAPACITY_RADIUS_FOLLOWS_SCOUT`, meaning "equal to scout_radius" (8), not a
; radius of zero. tiles_per_individual = 5 (D-45; D-43 originally shipped 3 — see D-45 in
; decisions.md for why: at 3, on the two most generic/shared tags in the game
; (open_grass + cultivated), Alpaca out-competed every other farm-tag species for the same
; land under the exclusivity rule's whole-radius-disc ownership, crowding out Horse/Donkey/
; Cow/Bull and triggering their Gentle Displacement. 5 matches Horse/Cow — no longer an
; outlier bargain against its own cluster. max_individuals = 6. Farm-tolerant.
; art.md's single-tag axis (open_grass) would have violated roster.md's own "≥ 2 tags" mix
; rule, so `cultivated` was added — alpacas are commonly kept alongside crops/pasture.
;
; fact_text is docs/content/cleared-pool-fact-cards.md § Alpaca's proposed line, transcribed
; verbatim — all four checklist steps PASS there.
;   "Baby alpacas are called crias" -> ADW Lama pacos, "Reproduction": "Crias is the term
;   used to designate alpaca offspring up to 6 months of age."
;   "grown alpacas hum to each other — especially when something around them changes" ->
;   ADW, "Communication and Perception": "The most common is the humming vocalization,
;   which is produced under a variety of circumstances, such as distress or a change in
;   the environment." ("distress" deliberately trimmed from the card — see the source
;   file's retrieval trace.)
; https://animaldiversity.org/accounts/Lama_pacos/
;
; news_reports intentionally empty — News Report pools for this pool are a separate, later
; purchase (not part of Content Pipeline step 4/5 for this dispatch).
;
; TIERS — RE-SPEC 2026-09-04 (habitat tiers).
;
; PROPOSAL, NOT A DECISION. Every divisor below is this design's own first-pass proposal
; awaiting human sign-off, per the project rule that all tuning values are the human's.
; Source: docs/superpowers/specs/2026-09-04-habitat-tiers-design.md § 9.
;
; THIS IS WHAT FIXES THE DEFECT this whole design exists for: Alpaca used to share the
; IDENTICAL `open_grass, cultivated` recipe with Horse, Cow and Bull. Single tier
; "highland": `barn*` `open_grass/5` `rocks/6` — `rocks` is the distinguisher (an alpaca is
; a highland animal), and the `barn*` gate was added in self-review: the original proposal
; had no building need at all and so failed its own Domesticated category test (spec § 9).
;
; The legacy flat fields (habitat_needs / tiles_per_individual / max_individuals) are LEFT
; IN PLACE and are now inert: `effective_tiers()` prefers `tiers` when non-empty. They are
; retained so a rollback is a one-line edit rather than a re-authoring.
[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="AnimalDefinition" load_steps=8 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/definitions/animal_definition.gd" id="1_schema"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/animals/alpaca/Alpaca.tscn" id="2_model"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/definitions/habitat_need.gd" id="3_need"]
[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/definitions/habitat_tier.gd" id="4_tier"]

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="need_highland_barn"]
script = ExtResource("3_need")
tag = "barn"
radius = 0
tiles_per_individual = 0

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="need_highland_grass"]
script = ExtResource("3_need")
tag = "open_grass"
radius = 0
tiles_per_individual = 5

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="need_highland_rocks"]
script = ExtResource("3_need")
tag = "rocks"
radius = 0
tiles_per_individual = 6

[sub_resource type="Resource" id="tier_highland"]
script = ExtResource("4_tier")
id = "highland"
needs = Array[Resource]([SubResource("need_highland_barn"), SubResource("need_highland_grass"), SubResource("need_highland_rocks")])
limits = Array[Resource]([])
max_individuals = 6
arrival_group_size = 1

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_schema")
id = "alpaca"
display_name = "Alpaca"
habitat_needs = Array[String](["open_grass", "cultivated"])
personality = "Bold"
avoids = Array[String]([])
farm_tolerant = true
scout_radius = 8
capacity_radius = 0
tiles_per_individual = 5
max_individuals = 6
tiers = Array[Resource]([SubResource("tier_highland")])
emits_tags = Array[String]([])
model_scenes = Array[PackedScene]([ExtResource("2_model")])
fact_text_pool = Array[String](["Baby alpacas are called crias, and grown alpacas hum to each other — especially when something around them changes."])
news_reports = Array[String]([])
